Race condition in xfrm_policy_bysel_ctx() where the inexact bin is pruned after releasing xfrm_policy_lock, allowing another thread to free the bin via kfree_rcu before the pruning completes, leading to use-after-free.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
spin_unlock_bh(&net->xfrm.xfrm_policy_lock);
if (bin && delete)
    xfrm_policy_inexact_prune_bin(bin);
Reason:
After releasing the lock, a window exists where another thread can acquire the lock, call __xfrm_policy_inexact_flush(), and free the bin via kfree_rcu. The subsequent call to xfrm_policy_inexact_prune_bin(bin) then accesses the freed bin, causing a use-after-free.

